[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Englund Gambit"]
[Variation "4.Qd5 f6"]
[ECO "A40"]
[Character "gambit,sharp"]
[Risk "high"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "development-lead,central-control"]

1. d4 e5 2. dxe5 Nc6 3. Nf3 Qe7 4. Qd5?! { The queen defends e5 and eyes the black pieces, but it can be hit by tempo moves. } 4... f6 { Attacks e5 again with a pawn, so the queen on d5 cannot hold it. }
5. e4 (5. exf6 Nxf6 6. Qb3 d5)
5... fxe5 { Takes the pawn back and opens the f-file. } 6. Nc3 6... Nf6 { Develops and attacks the queen on d5. [%cal Gf6d5] } 7. Qd1 7... Nd8 { Heads for e6, a good square where the knight shields the king. } 8. Nd5 8... Nxd5 { Trades off White's strongest piece. } 9. exd5 9... d6 { Opens the bishop on c8 and supports the e5 pawn. } *
